text: ['({T}: Add {B} or {G}.)', '({T}: Add {B}.)', '({T}: Add {G} or {U}.)', '({T}: Add {G}.)', '({T}: Add {R} or {W}.)', '({T}: Add {R}.)', '({T}: Add {U} or {R}.)', '({T}: Add {U}.)', '({T}: Add {W} or {B}.)', '({T}: Add {W}.)', 'All creatures have "At the beginning of your upkeep, destroy this creature unless you pay {1}."', 'All creatures have haste.', 'All lands are 1/1 creatures that are still lands.', "Amrou Kithkin can't be blocked by creatures with power 3 or greater.", "As Black Vise enters the battlefield, choose an opponent.\\nAt the beginning of the chosen player's upkeep, Black Vise deals X damage to that player, where X is the number of cards in their hand minus 4.", "As Call to Arms enters the battlefield, choose a color and an opponent.\\nWhite creatures get +1/+1 as long as the chosen color is the most common color among nontoken permanents the chosen player controls but isn't tied for most common.\\nWhen the chosen color isn't the most common color among nontoken permanents the chosen player controls or is tied for most common, sacrifice Call to Arms.", 'As Sol Grail enters the battlefield, choose a color.\\n{T}: Add one mana of the chosen color.', 'At end of combat, destroy all creatures blocking or blocked by Kjeldoran Frostbeast.', 'At end of combat, gain control of all creatures blocking The Wretched for as long as you control The Wretched.', "At the beginning of each player's upkeep, Storm World deals X damage to that player, where X is 4 minus the number of cards in their hand.", "At the beginning of each player's upkeep, destroy target nonartifact creature that player controls of their choice. It can't be regenerated.", "At the beginning of your upkeep, change Halfdane's base power and toughness to the power and toughness of target creature other than Halfdane until the end of your next upkeep.", 'At the beginning of your upkeep, choose flying, first strike, trample, or rampage 3. Gabriel Angelfire gains that ability until your next upkeep. (Whenever a creature with rampage 3 becomes blocked, it gets +3/+3 until end of turn for each creature blocking it beyond the first.)', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, if an opponent controls more lands than you, you may search your library for up to three basic land cards, reveal them, put them into your hand, then shuffle.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, put a pin counter on Voodoo Doll.\\nAt the beginning of your end step, if Voodoo Doll is untapped, destroy Voodoo Doll and it deals damage to you equal to the number of pin counters on it.\\n{X}{X}, {T}: Voodoo Doll deals damage equal to the number of pin counters on it to any target. X is the number of pin counters on Voodoo Doll.', "At the beginning of your upkeep, you may pay {R}{R}{R}. If you don't, tap Rohgahh of Kher Keep and all creatures named Kobolds of Kher Keep, then an opponent gains control of them.\\nCreatures you control named Kobolds of Kher Keep get +2/+2.", "Cast this spell only during an opponent's turn after their upkeep step.\\nUntap all lands you control.", 'Cast this spell only during combat before blockers are declared.\\nUntap target attacking creature and remove it from combat. Gain control of that creature until end of turn.', "Cast this spell only during the declare attackers step and only if you've been attacked this step.\\nDestroy target attacking creature.", "Cast this spell only during the declare attackers step and only if you've been attacked this step.\\nPrevent all damage that would be dealt to you this turn by attacking creatures.", "Chain Lightning deals 3 damage to any target. Then that player or that permanent's controller may pay {R}{R}. If the player does, they may copy this spell and may choose a new target for that copy.", "Choose one —\\n• Destroy target blue permanent.\\n• Return target Island to its owner's hand.", "Choose one —\\n• Destroy target red permanent.\\n• Return target Mountain to its owner's hand.", 'Choose one —\\n• Target player gains X life.\\n• Prevent the next X damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.', "Choose target creature. When that creature dies this turn, return a creature card from its owner's graveyard to the battlefield under the control of that creature's owner.", 'Cinder Storm deals 7 damage to any target.', 'Counter target creature spell.', 'Counter target spell unless its controller pays {1}.', "Counter target spell. At the beginning of your next main phase, add an amount of {C} equal to that spell's mana value.", "Creatures can't attack a player unless that player cast a spell or put a nontoken permanent onto the battlefield during their last turn.", 'Creatures you control get +2/+0 until end of turn.', "Creatures you control have horsemanship. (They can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship.)", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nProtection from black", 'Destroy all black creatures.', 'Destroy all nonblack creatures. Hellfire deals X plus 3 damage to you, where X is the number of creatures that died this way.', 'Destroy all tapped creatures.', 'Destroy target artifact or enchantment.', 'Destroy target creature with horsemanship.', 'Destroy target creature. Its owner gains 4 life.', 'Destroy target nonblack creature.', 'Destroy target permanent.', 'Discard X cards, then return a card from your graveyard to your hand for each card discarded this way. Exile Recall.', 'Divine Intervention enters the battlefield with two intervention counters on it.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, remove an intervention counter from Divine Intervention.\\nWhen you remove the last intervention counter from Divine Intervention, the game is a draw.', 'Draw a card for each tapped creature target opponent controls.', 'Draw three cards.', 'Enchant creature\\nAt the beginning of the upkeep of enchanted creature\'s controller, put a -0/-1 counter on that creature.\\nWhen enchanted creature dies, that creature\'s controller chooses a creature that Takklemaggot could enchant. If the player does, return Takklemaggot to the battlefield under your control attached to that creature. If they don\'t, return Takklemaggot to the battlefield under your control as a non-Aura enchantment. It loses "enchant creature" and gains "At the beginning of that player\'s upkeep, Takklemaggot deals 1 damage to that player."', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't attack.\\nPrevent all combat damage that would be dealt by enchanted creature.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +0/+2 and can't be the target of spells.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/-2.', 'Enchant creature\\nWhenever enchanted creature becomes tapped, put a -0/-2 counter on it.', 'Enchant land\\nEnchanted land is a Swamp.', "Except for creatures named Akron Legionnaire and artifact creatures, creatures you control can't attack.", "Exile All Hallow's Eve with two scream counters on it.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, if All Hallow's Eve is exiled with a scream counter on it, remove a scream counter from it. If there are no more scream counters on it, put it into your graveyard and each player returns all creature cards from their graveyard to the battlefield.", 'Exile two target nonartifact creatures. Ashes to Ashes deals 5 damage to you.', 'Famine deals 3 damage to each creature and each player.', 'Fire Ambush deals 3 damage to any target.', 'First strike', "First strike; legendary landwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a legendary land.)", 'First strike\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, destroy Cosmic Horror unless you pay {3}{B}{B}{B}. If Cosmic Horror is destroyed this way, it deals 7 damage to you.', 'First strike\\nOther Kobold creatures you control have first strike.', 'Flying', 'Flying, trample\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Palladia-Mors unless you pay {R}{G}{W}.', "Flying\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Arcades Sabboth unless you pay {G}{W}{U}.\\nEach untapped creature you control gets +0/+2 as long as it's not attacking.\\n{W}: Arcades Sabboth gets +0/+1 until end of turn.", 'Flying\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Nicol Bolas unless you pay {U}{B}{R}.\\nWhenever Nicol Bolas deals damage to an opponent, that player discards their hand.', 'Flying\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Vaevictis Asmadi unless you pay {B}{R}{G}.\\n{B}: Vaevictis Asmadi gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\\n{R}: Vaevictis Asmadi gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\\n{G}: Vaevictis Asmadi gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', "Flying\\nIf Firestorm Phoenix would die, return it to its owner's hand instead. Until that player's next turn, that player plays with that card revealed in their hand and can't play it.", 'Flying\\nOther Faerie creatures you control get +0/+1.\\n{T}: Other Faerie creatures you control get +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'Flying\\nRampage 2 (Whenever this creature becomes blocked, it gets +2/+2 until end of turn for each creature blocking it beyond the first.)\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Chromium unless you pay {W}{U}{B}.', 'Flying\\n{B}{R}{G}, {T}: Target player draws a card.', 'Flying\\n{G}, {T}: Add {R}.', 'Flying\\n{G}: Killer Bees gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Flying\\n{R}, {T}: Crimson Manticore deals 1 damage to target attacking or blocking creature.', 'Flying\\n{R}: Fire Drake gets +1/+0 until end of turn. Activate only once each turn.', 'Flying\\n{R}{G}, {T}: Target creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Forked Lightning deals 4 damage divided as you choose among one, two, or three target creatures.', 'Haste', "Haste; horsemanship (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship.)", "Horsemanship (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship.)", "Horsemanship (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship.)\\nLiu Bei, Lord of Shu gets +2/+2 as long as you control a permanent named Guan Yu, Sainted Warrior or a permanent named Zhang Fei, Fierce Warrior.", "Horsemanship (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship.)\\nSacrifice Xiahou Dun, the One-Eyed: Return target black card from your graveyard to your hand. Activate only during your turn, before attackers are declared.", "Horsemanship (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship.)\\nWhen Guan Yu, Sainted Warrior is put into your graveyard from the battlefield, you may shuffle Guan Yu into your library.", "Horsemanship (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship.)\\nWhen Sun Ce, Young Conquerer enters the battlefield, you may return target creature to its owner's hand.", "Horsemanship (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship.)\\nWhenever Lu Xun, Scholar General deals damage to an opponent, you may draw a card.", "Horsemanship (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship.)\\nWhenever Wei Night Raiders deals damage to an opponent, that player discards a card.", 'If an opponent who controls at least as many lands as you do would put a land onto the battlefield, that player instead puts that land onto the battlefield then sacrifices a land.', 'If target creature has toughness 5 or greater, it gets +4/-4 until end of turn. Otherwise, it gets +4/-X until end of turn, where X is its toughness minus 1.', "Jungle Lion can't block.", "Legendary creatures don't untap during their controllers' untap steps.\\nWhen Arena of the Ancients enters the battlefield, tap all legendary creatures.", 'Look at the top three cards of your library. Put one of them into your hand and the rest into your graveyard.', 'Minotaur creatures get +1/+0.', 'Other Kobold creatures you control get +0/+1 and have trample.', 'Other Kobold creatures you control get +1/+0.', 'Other creatures you control get +1/+1.', 'Other green creatures you control get +1/+1.', "Prevent the next 1 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", 'Protection from red\\nCreatures named Ivory Guardians get +1/+1 as long as an opponent controls a nontoken red permanent.', "Put target creature on top of its owner's library.", 'Rampage 1 (Whenever this creature becomes blocked, it gets +1/+1 until end of turn for each creature blocking it beyond the first.)', 'Rampage 2 (Whenever this creature becomes blocked, it gets +2/+2 until end of turn for each creature blocking it beyond the first.)', "Rasputin Dreamweaver enters the battlefield with seven dream counters on it.\\nRemove a dream counter from Rasputin: Add {C}.\\nRemove a dream counter from Rasputin: Prevent the next 1 damage that would be dealt to Rasputin this turn.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, if Rasputin started the turn untapped, put a dream counter on it.\\nRasputin can't have more than seven dream counters on it.", 'Return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.', "Return target permanent to its owner's hand.", 'Rolling Earthquake deals X damage to each creature without horsemanship and each player.', 'Sacrifice Loyal Retainers: Return target legendary creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield. Activate only during your turn, before attackers are declared.', "Sacrifice a creature: You gain life equal to the sacrificed creature's toughness. Activate only during your upkeep.", 'Search your library for a Forest card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for a Plains, Island, Swamp, Mountain, or Forest card and put that card onto the battlefield. Then shuffle.', 'Search your library for a card, put that card into your hand, then shuffle. You lose 3 life.', 'Stolen Grain deals 5 damage to target opponent or planeswalker. You gain 5 life.', 'Sword of the Ages enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Sword of the Ages and any number of creatures you control: Sword of the Ages deals X damage to any target, where X is the total power of the creatures sacrificed this way, then exile Sword of the Ages and those creature cards.', 'Take an extra turn after this one.', "Target creature gains first strike until end of turn.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", "Target creature gets +2/+0 until end of turn.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", "Target creature gets +2/+2 and gains horsemanship. (It can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship. This effect lasts indefinitely.)", 'Target creature gets +3/+3 until end of turn.', 'Target player discards X cards at random.', "Tetsuo Umezawa can't be the target of Aura spells.\\n{U}{B}{B}{R}, {T}: Destroy target tapped or blocking creature.", 'Trample\\nWhenever a creature dealt damage by Axelrod Gunnarson this turn dies, you gain 1 life and Axelrod deals 1 damage to target player or planeswalker.', "Untap target artifact, creature, or land.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", "Vigilance; horsemanship (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship.)", "Vigilance\\nBartel Runeaxe can't be the target of Aura spells.", 'When Corrupt Eunuchs enters the battlefield, it deals 2 damage to target creature.', "When Dance of Many enters the battlefield, create a token that's a copy of target nontoken creature.\\nWhen Dance of Many leaves the battlefield, exile the token.\\nWhen the token leaves the battlefield, sacrifice Dance of Many.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Dance of Many unless you pay {U}{U}.", 'When Dong Zhou, the Tyrant enters the battlefield, target creature an opponent controls deals damage equal to its power to that player.', 'When Hazezon Tamar enters the battlefield, create X 1/1 Sand Warrior creature tokens that are red, green, and white at the beginning of your next upkeep, where X is the number of lands you control at that time.\\nWhen Hazezon leaves the battlefield, exile all Sand Warriors.', 'When Shu Soldier-Farmers enters the battlefield, you gain 4 life.', 'When Stangg enters the battlefield, create Stangg Twin, a legendary 3/4 red and green Human Warrior creature token. Exile that token when Stangg leaves the battlefield. Sacrifice Stangg when that token leaves the battlefield.', 'When Zodiac Dragon is put into your graveyard from the battlefield, you may return it to your hand.', "When you cast this spell, counter it unless you sacrifice a land.\\nAt the beginning of each player's upkeep, that player sacrifices a land.\\nWhen there are no lands on the battlefield, sacrifice Mana Vortex.", 'Whenever Hunting Cheetah deals damage to an opponent, you may search your library for a Forest card, reveal that card, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', "Whenever Labyrinth Minotaur blocks a creature, that creature doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.", 'Whenever Slashing Tiger becomes blocked, it gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', "Whenever a permanent becomes tapped, put a wind counter on it.\\nIf a permanent with a wind counter on it would untap during its controller's untap step, remove all wind counters from it instead.", 'Whenever a player casts a spell, counter it unless that player pays {3}.', "Wu Warship can't attack unless defending player controls an Island.", 'You destroy four lands you control, then target opponent destroys four lands they control. Then Burning of Xinye deals 4 damage to each creature.', 'You gain 2 life for each creature you control.', "You may choose not to untap Old Man of the Sea during your untap step.\\n{T}: Gain control of target creature with power less than or equal to Old Man of the Sea's power for as long as Old Man of the Sea remains tapped and that creature's power remains less than or equal to Old Man of the Sea's power.", 'You may choose not to untap Rubinia Soulsinger during your untap step.\\n{T}: Gain control of target creature for as long as you control Rubinia and Rubinia remains tapped.', 'You may choose not to untap Willow Satyr during your untap step.\\n{T}: Gain control of target legendary creature for as long as you control Willow Satyr and Willow Satyr remains tapped.', "Young Wei Recruits can't block.", "{0}: You may put a basic Forest card from your hand onto the battlefield. Activate only as a sorcery and only once each turn.\\nSacrifice Gaea's Touch: Add {G}{G}.", "{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Astrolabe: Add two mana of any one color. Draw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", '{1}: Carrion Ants gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', '{1}{W}, {T}: Destroy target black creature.', '{2}, {T}: All creatures get -1/-0 until end of turn.', "{2}, {T}: Exile the top card of your library face down.\\n{0}: Sacrifice Knowledge Vault. If you do, discard your hand, then put all cards exiled with Knowledge Vault into their owner's hand.\\nWhen Knowledge Vault leaves the battlefield, put all cards exiled with Knowledge Vault into their owner's graveyard.", '{2}{B}{R}, {T}: Create a 1/1 black and red Demon creature token named Minor Demon.', '{3}, Sacrifice Coal Golem: Add {R}{R}{R}.', "{3}, {T}: The next time a source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, that damage is dealt to target creature of an opponent's choice instead.", "{3}: Target creature doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.", '{3}: You may put a Minotaur permanent card from your hand onto the battlefield.', '{5}, Sacrifice Gauntlets of Chaos: Exchange control of target artifact, creature, or land you control and target permanent an opponent controls that shares one of those types with it. If those permanents are exchanged this way, destroy all Auras attached to them.', "{B}: If Lesser Werewolf's power is 1 or more, it gets -1/-0 until end of turn and put a -0/-1 counter on target creature blocking or blocked by Lesser Werewolf. Activate only during the declare blockers step.", '{B}{R}: Pavel Maliki gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', '{G}{G}, {T}: Tracker deals damage equal to its power to target creature. That creature deals damage equal to its power to Tracker.', "{G}{G}: Wormwood Treefolk gains forestwalk until end of turn and deals 2 damage to you. (It can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Forest.)\\n{B}{B}: Wormwood Treefolk gains swampwalk until end of turn and deals 2 damage to you. (It can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Swamp.)", '{G}{W}{U}, {T}: Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt this turn. Activate only before the combat damage step.', '{G}{W}{U}, {T}: Regenerate target creature.', '{T}, Exile a creature you control: Put a storage counter on City of Shadows.\\n{T}: Add {C} for each storage counter on City of Shadows.', '{T}, Untap a tapped land an opponent controls: Add one mana of any type that land could produce.', '{T}: Add one mana of any color that a land an opponent controls could produce.', '{T}: Add {B}.', '{T}: Add {B}. Elves of Deep Shadow deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {B}.\\n{T}: Target creature loses first strike or swampwalk until end of turn.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}.', '{T}: Add {R}.\\n{T}: Target creature loses all landwalk abilities until end of turn.', '{T}: Add {U}.', "{T}: Add {W}.\\n{T}: Return target legendary creature to its owner's hand.", '{T}: Another target Minotaur creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', "{T}: Choose two target blocking creatures an opponent controls. If each of those creatures could block all creatures that the other is blocking, remove both of them from combat. Each one then blocks all creatures the other was blocking.\\nWhenever Sorrow's Path becomes tapped, it deals 2 damage to you and each creature you control.", "{T}: D'Avenant Archer deals 1 damage to target attacking or blocking creature.", '{T}: Destroy target enchanted creature.', '{T}: Draw two cards, then discard three cards.', '{T}: Lady Caleria deals 3 damage to target attacking or blocking creature.', '{T}: Prevent the next 2 damage that would be dealt to target creature this turn.', '{T}: Put target creature card from your graveyard on top of your library. Activate only during your turn, before attackers are declared.', "{T}: Reveka, Wizard Savant deals 2 damage to any target and doesn't untap during your next untap step.", '{T}: Target creature gets -1/-0 until end of turn.', '{T}: Target player discards a card at random. Activate only during your turn.', '{T}: Tor Wauki deals 2 damage to target attacking or blocking creature.', '{T}: Wu Longbowman deals 1 damage to any target. Activate only during your turn, before attackers are declared.', '{T}: You may put a Faerie permanent card from your hand onto the battlefield.\\n{2}{G}: Target green creature gains protection from black until end of turn.', '{U}: Regenerate Spiny Starfish.\\nAt the beginning of each end step, if Spiny Starfish regenerated this turn, create a 0/1 blue Starfish creature token for each time it regenerated this turn.', '{W}, Pay 1 life: Prevent the next 2 damage that would be dealt to target creature this turn.\\n{U}: Prevent the next 1 damage that would be dealt to target Cleric or Wizard creature this turn.\\n{B}, Put a -1/-1 counter on a creature you control: Prevent the next 2 damage that would be dealt to target player or planeswalker this turn.', '{W}{B}, {T}: Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt by target creature this turn.', '{X}, {T}: Banshee deals half X damage, rounded down, to any target, and half X damage, rounded up, to you.', '{X}, {T}: Choose a card name. Target opponent reveals X cards at random from their hand. Then that player discards all cards with that name revealed this way. Activate only during your turn.', "{X}: You may choose a creature card in your hand whose mana cost could be paid by some amount of, or all of, the mana you spent on {X}. If you do, you may cast that card face down as a 2/2 creature spell without paying its mana cost. If the creature that spell becomes as it resolves has not been turned face up and would assign or deal damage, be dealt damage, or become tapped, instead it's turned face up and assigns or deals damage, is dealt damage, or becomes tapped. Activate only as a sorcery."]
flavor: ['"\'Tis distance lends enchantment to the view,/ And robes the mountain in its azure hue."\\n—Thomas Campbell, "Pleasures of Hope"', '"\'War is no picnic,\' my father liked to say. But the ants seemed to disagree."\\n—General Chanek Valteroth', '". . . The kingdoms three are now the stuff of dream,/ For men to ponder, past all praise or blame."', '"All men have their appointed time; that\'s something no horse can change."\\n—Liu Bei, after being told that the Dilu brings its master ill fortune', '"All rivers eventually run to the sea. My job is to sort out who goes first."\\n—Maeveen O\'Donagh, Memoirs of a Soldier', '"All warfare is based on deception."\\n—Sun Tzu, Art of War (trans. Giles)', '"An immense river of oblivion is sweeping us away into a nameless abyss."\\n—Ernest Renan, Souvenirs d\'Enfance et de Jeunesse', '"Battles no longer served a purpose in Karakas."\\n—Angus Mackenzie, Diary', '"But it was a year of dearth. People were reduced to eating leaves of jujube trees. Corpses were seen everywhere in the countryside."', '"Dong Zhuo\'s man, Lu Bu, warrior without peer,/ Far surpassed the champions of his sphere."', '"Faeries talk all in riddles and tricky bits, \'cept the Nobles. Now, there\'s some straight talkers."\\n—Joskun, An-Havva Constable', '"He Guan Yu covered the ground on a thousand-li horse;/ With dragon blade he took each pass by force."', '"Healing is a matter of time, but it is sometimes also a matter of opportunity."\\n—D\'Avenant proverb', '"High on a throne of royal state . . . insatiate to pursue vain war with heav\'n."\\n—John Milton, Paradise Lost', '"How can you accuse me of evil? Though these deeds be unsavory, no one will argue: good shall follow from them."', '"I do not remember what he said to her. I remember her fiery eyes, fixed upon him for an instant. I remember a flash, and the hot breath of sudden flames made me turn away. When I looked again, Angus was gone."\\n—A Wayfarer, on meeting Lady Orca', '"I doubt any labyrinth minotaurs still live—but then again, we minotaurs are stubborn beings."\\n—Onatah, Anaba Shaman', '"If you do it right, they\'ll never know what hit them."\\n—General Jarkeld, the Arctic Fox', '"It\'s nice to see a sister Dwarf in a position of such power, but why\'d it have to be one of those seafaring muleheads?"\\n—Halina, Dwarven Trader', '"Joining this army is easy, boy. Just survive your first battle."', '"Kobolds are harmless."\\n—Bearand the Bold, epitaph', '"Leadership, not numbers, determines victory."\\n—A Wu commander, before his 5,000 troops forced 15,000 Wei troops to retreat from Ruxu', '"Lieutenants dishonored, corpses carted home; The general raises troops again to take revenge."', '"Look deep into the Grail, and see there what you desire most."\\n—Gerda Äagesdotter, Archmage of the Unseen', '"O! call back yesterday, bid time return."\\n—William Shakespeare, King Richard the Second', '"On the field of honor, a soldier need have no fear."', '"One for all, all for one; we strike first, and then you\'re done!"\\n—Oath of the Kobold Musketeers', '"One score and four he reigned, the Southland king: / A dragon coiled, a tiger poised below the mighty Yangtze."', '"Only wisdom and virtue can truly win men\'s devotion."\\n—Liu Bei', '"Plans evolved within the tent decide a victory 1,000 li away."', '"Play the song of he who delivered us. Play the song of Feroz."\\n—Onatah, Anaba Shaman', '"Political violence is a perfectly legitimate answer to the persecution handed down by dignitaries of the state."', '"Remember Sir Shandlar! Remember and stand firm!"\\n—rallying cry of the Eberyn militia', '"Resignedly beneath the sky/The melancholy waters lie./So blend the turrets and shadows there/That all seem pendulous in air,/While from a proud tower in town/Death looks gigantically down."\\n—Edgar Allan Poe, "The City in the Sea"', '"Sometimes even the smallest boon can save a life."\\n—Halvor Arenson, Kjeldoran Priest', '"Such a lord as this—all virtues\' height—Had never been, nor ever was again."', '"The Ancestors are the wisdom of the tribe and the soul of the Homelands. I am eternally in their debt."\\n—Taysir', '"The Spirit Crafters sing of all our people. They sing of those lost, of those found, and of those who are yet to be."\\n—Onatah, Anaba Shaman', '"The bird of wonder dies, the maiden phoenix,/ Her ashes new-create another heir/ As great in admiration as herself."\\n—William Shakespeare, King Henry the Eighth', '"The burst of strength brought on by this plague should not be mistaken for a sign of renewed health."\\n—Kolbjörn, High Honored Druid', '"The potential for change lies in all things. Know a thing\'s nature, know its possibilities, and know it anew."\\n—Gustha Ebbasdotter, Kjeldoran Royal Mage', '"Then flashed the living lightning from her eyes,/ And screams of horror rend th\' affrighted skies."\\n—Alexander Pope, The Rape of the Lock', '"Those of faith are those of strength."\\n—Autumn Willow', '"Three such creatures stood burning at the crest of the hill. Only seconds later, the fireball struck our front line."\\n—Lydia, Countess Brellis', '"To make a prairie it takes a clover and one bee,/ One clover, and a bee,/ And revery."\\n—Emily Dickinson', '"To send the common people to war untrained is to throw them away."\\n—Confucius, The Analects (trans. Lau)', '"Trying to meet a worthy man in the wrong way is as bad as closing the door on an invited guest."\\n—Mencius, a Chinese philosopher', '"Two of my Warriors found that the creature was dangerous not only in combat, but also in simple proximity."\\n—Disa the Restless, journal entry', '"Unless you enter the tiger\'s lair, you cannot get hold of the tiger\'s cubs."\\n—Sun Tzu, Art of War (trans. Giles)', '"We three, though of separate ancestry, join in brotherhood. . . . We dare not hope to be together always but hereby vow to die the selfsame day."\\n—Peach Garden Oath', '"What can be a stronger shield than concealment? Have you ever defeated an enemy you didn\'t know existed?"\\n—Gerda Äagesdotter, Archmage of the Unseen', '"What do you have that I cannot obtain?"\\n—Mairsil, called the Pretender', '"When milady was young, the sight of a rainbow would fill her soul with peace. As she grew, she learned to share her rapture with others."\\n—Lady Gabriella', '"With fire he broke the battle at Bowang . . . . Striking fear deep into Cao Cao\'s soul, thus Kongming scored a coup at his debut."', '"You would never guess, at the terrifying sight of the man, that Hunding was as charming a companion as one could wish for."', 'A regular guest at the Royal Masquerade, Arien is the envy of the Court. She appears in a new costume every hour.', 'Administrator of the military state of Sheoltun, Tobias is the military right arm of the empire and the figurehead of its freedom.', "After the Battle of Pitdown, Lady Ursnell fashioned the first such instrument out of Lord Ursnell's left leg.", 'An explorer of the Æther, Tuknir often discovers himself in the most unusual physical realms.', "As many attackers were dazzled by the wall's beauty as were halted by its force.", 'As the Wu chief commander, Lu Meng conquered Shu-held Jingzhou in 219 by disguising soldiers as merchants on boats filled with hiding troops.', 'At Red Cliffs, Kongming and Zhou Yu each wrote his plan for defeating Wei on the palm of his hand. They laughed as they both revealed the same word, "Fire."', "At the battle of Chang'an, Ma Chao defeated the two generals Cao Cao sent to guard the pass but was forced to flee when Cao Cao's trickery turned his own ally against him.", 'At the battle of Guandu, Cao Cao defeated Yuan Shao by raiding his grain depot, leaving him with no way to feed his troops.', "At the second battle of Ruxu, the brave Wu general Gan Ning raided Cao Cao's camp of 400,000 men with only 100 cavalry. Not a single man or horse was lost.", "Avenant's archers are also trained as poets, so that each arrow is guided by a fragment of verse.", 'Both Wu and Wei warships patrolled the Yangtze River, the natural border between the two kingdoms.', "Brimstone marks this drake's territory. Unfortunately for travelers, all of the Burning Isles smell likewise.", 'Cao Cao was haunted to death by the ghosts of the empresses and other high courtiers he had murdered.', 'Cao Cao was more concerned with capabilities than lineage. He excelled at recruiting and retaining men of talent to serve him.', "During Kongming's campaigns against the Wei, his Shu troops rotated from the battlefront to the fields every hundred days.", "Even the brave have cause to tremble at the sight of Sivitri Scarzam. Who else has tamed Scarzam's Dragon?", "For a dozen years the Cage had held Lord Ith, but as the Pretender Mairsil's power weakened, so did the bars.", "Hail from Tolaria the ever changing 'Dane.", 'He is devious and cunning, in both appearance and deed. Beware the Warbeard, for this brute bites as well as he barks!', 'Her given name has been lost in the mists of time. Legend says that her silent vigil will one day be ended by the one who, pure of heart and spirit, calls out that name again.', "In establishing the Shu kingdom, Liu Bei's forces fought against Ma Chao at Chengdu. Eventually, Ma Chao surrendered and became one of Liu Bei's Tiger Generals.", 'Kher Keep is unique among fortresses: impervious to aerial assault but defenseless from the ground.', 'Kongming and Lu Su tricked Wei troops into shooting over 100,000 arrows at them to later use against the Wei at Red Cliffs.', "Livonya's own nature is a matter of mystery. Nothing is known for sure, merely rumors of unearthly stealth, and unholy alliances.", 'Many people say that no power can bring the mountains low. Many people are fools.', 'Marhault Elsdragon follows a strict philosophy, never letting emotions cloud his thoughts. No chance observer could imagine the rage in his heart.', 'Mightiest of the cat warriors, Jedit Ojanen forsook the forests of his tribe and took service with the Robaran Mercenaries, rising through their ranks to lead them in the battle for Efrava.', 'Nethya stiffened suddenly, head cocked as if straining to hear some distant sound, then felt lifeless to the ground.', 'Noted neither for their good looks nor their charm, manticores can be fearsome allies. As dinner companions, however, they are best left alone.', "Once, the order of the Closed Fist reached throughout the Kb'Briann Highlands. Now, Jerrard alone remains to uphold their standard.", 'One who goes unpunished never learns.\\n—Greek proverb', 'Quick and agile, Amrou Kithkin can usually escape from even the most fearsome opponents.', 'Ramirez DePietro is a most flamboyant pirate. Be careful not to believe his tall tales, especially when you ask his age.', 'Some say Banshees are the hounds of Death, baying to herd their prey into the arms of their master.', 'Sunastian has roots in both sorcery and swordplay; he has learned never to depend too heavily on the latter.', 'The Taskmaster knows that there is no cure for the common Kobold.', "The clouds broke and the sun's rays burst forth; each foul beast in its turn faltered, and was gone.", 'The communal mind produces a savage strategy, yet no one could predict that this vicious crossbreed would unravel the secret of steel.', 'The elite guard of the Mesa High Priests, the Ivory Guardians, were created to protect the innocent and faithful. Some say their actions are above the law.', 'The frost giants have been out in the cold a long, long time, but they have their rage to keep them warm.', "The lion's only loyalty is to its hunger.", 'The minotaurs of the Hurloon Mountains are known for their love of battle. They are also known for their hymns to the dead, sung for friend and foe alike. These hymns can last for days, filling the mountain valleys with their low, haunting sounds.', 'The mourning families of commanders and generals were often given land, valuables, or money to compensate for their losses.', "The only sound was the gentle clicking of the faeries' wings. Then those intruders who were still standing turned and fled. One thing was certain: they didn't think the scryb were very funny anymore.", 'The only thing worse than a minotaur with an axe is an angry minotaur with an axe.', 'The province of Jingzhou was the fulcrum of the three kingdoms. At separate times it was coveted and controlled by the Wu, the Shu, and the Wei.', 'The rising oceans brought new lakes—and new terrors—to Terisiare. The Explorers found their ancient enemies spawning everywhere.', 'The stubborn Meng Huo was captured and released by Kongming seven times before finally surrendering.', 'The voices of the dead ring in the heart long after they have faded from the ears.', 'These days, some wizards are finding that they have a little too much spell left at the end of their mana.', 'They are aberrations who have turned on everything we hold sacred. Let them be cast out."\\n—Ailheen, Speaker of the Council', 'Though they often bore little greater charm than the demons they battled, exorcists were always welcome in Scarwood.', 'Through his allies, Meng Huo commanded several hundred thousand troops composed of cavalry, rattan-armored warriors, infantry, naked men with swords, and wild animals.', 'Throughout the three kingdoms, important generals were often guarded by small groups of expert soldiers known as "elite companions."', "Thundering down from Hammerheim, no foe could slow Bartel's charge.", 'Trip wire, hooked poles, and sunken pits were commonly used to unhorse riders during the Three Kingdoms period.', 'Urborg became the final resting place of many swordsmen of renown, their steel outmatched by the wiles of Gwendlyn.', 'We all know the legend: Pavel wanders the realms, helping those in greatest need. But is this a measure of his generosity, or of his obligation to atone?', 'Wei won the battle of Hefei when Zhang Liao defeated Sun Quan and then foiled a Wu scheme to incite rebellion.', "When the sky's rain has turned to fire, what will put it out?", "Zhang Fei's uncharacteristic alliance with a defeated Riverlands general, Yan Yan, allowed Shu forces to advance through forty-five Riverlands strongpoints with no casualties."]
artist: ['Alan Rabinowitz', 'Amy Weber', 'Andi Rusu', 'Anson Maddocks', 'Anthony S. Waters', 'Brian Snõddy', 'Bryon Wackwitz', 'Chen Weidong', 'Christopher Rush', 'Cornelius Brudi', 'Dan Frazier', 'Daniel Gelon', 'DiTerlizzi', 'Douglas Shuler', 'Drew Tucker', 'Edward P. Beard, Jr.', 'Fang Yue', 'Gao Jianzhang', 'Gao Yan', 'Greg Simanson', 'Harold McNeill', 'He Jiancheng', 'Hong Yan', 'Huang Qishi', 'Inoue Junichi', 'Jack Wei', 'Janine Johnston', 'Jeff A. Menges', 'Jesper Myrfors', 'Ji Yong', 'Jiaming', 'Jiang Zhuqing', 'Julie Baroh', 'Junko Taguchi', 'Justin Hampton', 'Kang Yu', 'Ku Xueming', 'LHQ', 'Li Tie', 'Li Wang', 'Li Xiaohua', 'Li Youliang', 'Li Yousong', 'Liu Shangying', 'Liz Danforth', 'Margaret Organ-Kean', 'Mark Poole', 'Mark Tedin', 'Melissa A. Benson', 'Nicola Leonard', 'NéNé Thomas', 'Pete Venters', 'Phil Foglio', 'Qi Baocheng', 'Qiao Dafu', 'Qin Jun', 'Qu Xin', 'Quinton Hoover', 'Randy Asplund-Faith', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Richard Kane Ferguson', 'Richard Thomas', 'Rob Alexander', 'Sandra Everingham', 'Scott Kirschner', 'Scott M. Fischer', 'Shang Huitong', 'Solomon Au Yeung', 'Song Shikai', 'Sun Nan', 'Susan Van Camp', 'Tang Xiaogu', 'Ted Naifeh', 'Tom Wänerstrand', 'Wang Chuxiong', 'Wang Feng', 'Xu Tan', 'Xu Xiaoming', 'Yang Guangmai', 'Yang Hong', 'Yang Jun Kwon', 'Zhang Jiazhen']
